":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A custom keyboard extension may sometimes have to open URLs or trigger deep links, for instance to open the app or System Settings. Since it can’t access ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UIApplication.shared"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", opening URLs can be difficult.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit provides ways to open URLs from a keyboard without ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UIApplication.shared"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":". You can use this to open any URL with ease.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Opening-a-URL-from-a-Keyboard-Extension","level":2,"text":"Opening a URL from a Keyboard Extension"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The best way to open a URL from a keyboard extension, is to use a native SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Link","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". You can also trigger a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/url(_:id:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" action to let the main ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardServices\/actionHandler","type":"reference"},{"text":" open it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS 26 and later requires Full Access to open URLs with both native links and a "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardActionHandler","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". You should ask the user to enable Full Access if you need to open URLs from your keyboard."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Opening-System-Settings","level":2,"text":"Opening System Settings"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit defines a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Foundation\/URL\/systemSettings","type":"reference"},{"text":" URL that can be used to open your app in System Settings. This can be used to help users enable the keyboard, enable Full Access, etc.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"tip","name":"Tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your keyboard navigates to the System Settings root instead of your app, try adding an empty settings bundle to your app target."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Opening-the-Main-App-from-a-Keyboard-Extension","level":2,"text":"Opening the Main App from a Keyboard Extension"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The best way to open the main app from a keyboard extension, is to trigger the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/openMainApp(_:withReason:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" action to let the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardServices\/actionHandler","type":"reference"},{"text":" open it. You can provide an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReason","type":"reference"},{"text":" to tell the app why it was opened.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In your main app target, you can then use the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext","type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext\/openReason","type":"reference"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext\/openReasonCase","type":"reference"},{"text":" as an indication that the app was opened from your keyboard extension.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The open reason will automatically reset when the main app is sent to the background, which means that you can automatically hide this message when it’s no longer needed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"aside","style":"tip","name":"Tip","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit will automatically open your main app with the open reason "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReason\/dictation","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" when starting dictation, then try to navigate back to the keyboard once dictation has been started."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Returning-to-the-Keyboard-Extension","level":2,"text":"Returning to the Keyboard Extension"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext","type":"reference"},{"text":" has a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardContext\/hostApplicationBundleId","type":"reference"},{"text":" (see the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","type":"reference"},{"text":" article for more information) that can be mapped to a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplicationProvider\/hostApplication","type":"reference"},{"text":", you can trigger the app’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication\/open(withAction:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" to return to the keyboard.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"However, since KeyboardKit only knows about the most common apps, you can’t rely on this. You should therefore instruct your users on how to tap the top leading back button to return to the keyboard, when no ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplicationProvider\/hostApplication","type":"reference"},{"text":" is available.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can read more in the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","type":"reference"},{"text":" article. This article also has information on adding more ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardHostApplication","type":"reference"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"Navigation","roleHeading":"Article","images":[{"type":"card","identifier":"Feature-Navigation.jpg"}],"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the KeyboardKit navigation engine.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Types","title":"Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/UrlOpener"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit/documentation/KeyboardKit/Feedback-Article":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"This article describes the KeyboardKit feedback engine.","type":"text"}],"title":"Feedback","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.keyboardkit.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Feedback-Article","url":"\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/feedback-article","type":"topic","kind":"article","images":[{"type":"card","identifier":"Feature-Feedback.jpg"}]},"doc://com.keybo